==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*bogъ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|phon=бох}}
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|Ru-бог.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}

In the nominative singular, the word is usually pronounced {{IPAchar|/box/}} (as if spelled {{lang|ru|бох}}) due to Church Slavonic influence. The regular pronunciation {{IPAchar|/bok/}} is used only rarely. In all other case forms, the regular {{IPAchar|/ɡ/}} is more common, but older pronunciations used {{IPAchar|/ɣ/}}.

===Noun===
{{ru-noun|бог|m-an|tr=box|бо́га|бо́ги|f=боги́ня}}

# [[God]]
# [[god]], [[idol]]
#: {{lang|ru|бог [[он|его́]] [[знать|зна́ет]]!}} — ''God only knows!; goodness knows!''
#: {{lang|ru|[[боже|бо́же]] [[мой]]!}} — ''oh God!; good gracious!''
#: {{lang|ru|бог [[с#Russian|с]] [[он|ним]]!}} — ''Forget him!''
#: {{lang|ru|[[давать|дай]] бог!}} — ''God willing!; let’s hope so!''
#: {{lang|ru|[[ей-богу|ей-бо́гу]]!}} — ''really!; really and truly!''
#: {{lang|ru|[[ради|ра́ди]] бо́га!}} — ''for God’s sake!''
#: {{lang|ru|[[сохранять|сохрани́]] [[боже|бо́же]]!}} — ''God forbid!''
#: {{lang|ru|[[слава богу|сла́ва бо́гу]]!}} — ''thank God!''

====Usage notes====
* Usually not capitalized in Russian in the sense of [[idol]], or when referring to a single god with a polytheistic pantheon. Capitalized in monotheistic sense, such as in Islamic or Christian discourse.

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|e|voc=бо́же|a=an}}

